From: Aurélien Pommel <aurelien.pommel@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: take the card number from a "sound" alias

Card numbers follow probe order, but stock-built software expects the codec
as card 0, ALSA's default device, as on the vendor kernel.

---
--- a/sound/soc/soc-core.c
+++ b/sound/soc/soc-core.c
@@ -2031,7 +2031,9 @@
 		goto probe_end;
 
 	/* card bind complete so register a sound card */
-	ret = snd_card_new(card->dev, SNDRV_DEFAULT_IDX1, SNDRV_DEFAULT_STR1,
+	ret = of_alias_get_id(card->dev->of_node, "sound");
+	ret = snd_card_new(card->dev, ret < 0 ? SNDRV_DEFAULT_IDX1 : ret,
+			SNDRV_DEFAULT_STR1,
 			card->owner, 0, &card->snd_card);
 	if (ret < 0) {
 		dev_err(card->dev,
